{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and afterwards may consider only specified convictions following an individualized assessment. Only a substantial, legitimate, nondiscriminatory interest justifies withdrawing an offer.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; providers may consider methamphetamine-manufacture convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), up to $5,000 (one prior), or up to $10,000 (two or more priors in seven years); director may order compliance actions and pay the applicant up to $1,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is part of its eligibility criteria and that the applicant may submit evidence of record inaccuracies or rehabilitation. The director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require the applicant's rental application fee be returned; monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 according to prior violations in the preceding five or seven years.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful housing provider appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and the court overturns the director's order, the provider may evict the former applicant placed in the unit under that order, with at least 45 days' notice before eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of a director's order under this act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Former applicant housed under a Division on Civil Rights order"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.)","confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
